{"type": "thinking", "text": "In Notes mode, sort options include note fields plus Deck, Due, Avg Ease, Card Modified, Created, Note Modified. Note Type, Cards, Tags. Looks plausible for notes mode. In cards mode, sort fields would be Sort Field, Card Type, Due, Deck, etc. Hmm, note sort includes \"Note Modified\". Fine.\n\nWait: In notes mode, the columns shown were Sort Field, Note Type, Cards, Tags. So sort by Deck/Due etc. allowed. OK.\n\nNow, is \"Change display order\" per mode? The current radio \"Sort Field ascending\" checked. Let me choose something like Tags descending? Better not alter data (sort setting is a app pref; testing requires). We can test and revert.\n\nHmm, I might be going down the wrong path. Let me focus: maybe the injected bug for the toggle is that the display columns in Notes mode are read from the Cards settings place — but they're not (we see correct). Unless... the browser's header showed correct notes columns but the row data under them? Row: \"agua | Basic | 1\" — Sort Field=agua, Note Type=Basic, Cards=1, Tags empty. Correct. And comer has verb tag. Correct.\n\nHmm OK. So maybe the bug is in the truncate/ignore accents sharing. Let me test toggling \"Ignore accents\" in one mode and see if it affects the other. Both are prefs; if shared, expected? Honestly, I'd expect \"Ignore accents in search\" to be global (search behavior global). So sharing is fine.\n\nWait, maybe I should look at this from the \"one shared place\" angle differently: it might describe a real upstream refactor where `CardsOrNotes` mode settings were centralized, and the injected bug is that the mode preference is read from the same place as something else, e.g., selecting Notes saves the wrong value, so next open shows Cards? We tested persistence once (saved Notes → reopened showed Notes). Good.\n\nCould the bug be that the toggle changes mode but the toolbar label still says the other mode? No.\n\nOK, maybe the bug in the cards/notes toggle only manifests in specific combos, e.g., toggling to Notes then using \"Add\" or navigating to a note, then back. Or rotation. Let me park this and test other areas, then return with fresh eyes.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider: \"each mode's display settings are now read from one shared place.\" Perhaps the bug is that display settings are read from a shared place *when they shouldn't be*, so the visible columns in Notes mode are actually from the cards configuration... but they're not. Unless the browser list reads columns correctly but the \"Manage columns\" save writes to the cards configuration. Test: add a column to Notes (e.g., include \"Deck\" in notes), save; then switch to Cards and verify Cards columns unchanged; then switch back. If including Deck in notes actually modifies cards' columns (since shared), that would be visible. Let's test that. Currently in Change display order overlay; close it by tapping outside/back."}
