n Notes mode. This tests persistence and rotation.\n\nBut I've done many toggles; each seems right.\n\nAlternative: maybe the bug in cards/notes is that the *columns* shown in the browser come from the shared place but the *header sort* uses the other mode's columns. Hmm.\n\nWait! I just realized something. Look at the \"Manage column\" popup when tapping a header in Notes mode: it listed \"Question\", \"Answer\", \"Deck\", \"Due\", \"Avg. Ease\", \"Card Modified\", \"Created\", \"Note Modified\", \"Avg. Interval\", \"Lapses\", \"Reviews\". But wait, in the *Cards* mode \"Manage column\" popup, what does it list? If both modes' popups list the same shared set (e.g., both list note fields), that's the shared-place bug. I haven't checked the Cards-mode popup. Actually earlier I only tapped header in Notes mode. In Cards mode, tapping \"Deck\" header would open the same popup; if it lists notes fields only (Question/Answer) that'd be wrong? Both modes' available columns likely overlap; hard to distinguish.\n\nHmm, the \"Manage column\" popup is maybe a generic list of all columns available to the mode. For notes mode, it should list note-specific columns (Question, Answer...). For cards mode, should list card-specific columns (Question? maybe not). Let's test: In Cards mode, tap \"Deck\" header and see the list. If it shows \"Note Type\"/\"Cards\" (notes-specific), that's the bug. This is promising since the hint says \"each mode's display settings are now read from one shared place\" — maybe the header popup reads the shared column list.\n\nLet me cancel this tag dialog first. Then switch to Cards mode, save, and tap a header.\n\nActually, we're in Cards mode already (last saved Cards). The current browser is Cards mode. Cancel the tag dialog [10]."}
