{"type": "thinking", "text": "Cards mode popup lists: Question, Answer, Tags, Ease, Card Modified, Created, Note Modified, Interval, Lapses, Note Type, Reviews. Notes mode popup listed: Question, Answer, Deck, Due, Avg. Ease, Card Modified, Created, Note Modified, Avg. Interval, Lapses, Reviews. These differ appropriately (Ease/Interval vs Avg Ease/Avg Interval; Note Type vs Deck/Due). Looks mode-specific and correct. So that's not the bug.\n\nHmm.\n\nCancel [12].\n\nLet me approach from \"what can be visibly wrong?\" Maybe I should check the deck list overflow options and the deck info screen. Or the \"Check\" database.\n\nActually, maybe the injected bugs are:\n1. Add note deck chooser sorting: BROKEN in a way only visible with more decks—we tested and it worked... unless the bug is that it sorts by full name but **ignores case**, and \"Aaa\" vs \"Sub\"? no.\n2. Deck arrows: maybe the arrow *icon* is correct but tapping the arrow also *opens the deck*? We tapped arrow and it only expanded, no navigation. Fine.\n3. Cards/notes: maybe the checkbox sharing is indeed the bug (truncate/ignore accents shared across modes, while expected separate). Hmm.\n\nLet me look up actual AnkiDroid source *from memory* more rigorously. AnkiDroid's BrowserOptions (2.16.5) layout `browser_options.xml` includes:\n- RadioGroup `cards_notes_radio_group` with `select_cards_mode`, `select_notes_mode`\n- `truncate_check_box`\n- `ignore_accents_check_box`\n- `manage_columns_button`\n- rename flags.\n\nIn `BrowserOptions.java`:\n```java\nmTruncateCheckBox.setChecked(prefs.getBoolean(Prefs.BROWSER_TRUNCATE_CONTENT, false));\nmIgnoreAccentsCheckBox.setChecked(prefs.getBoolean(Prefs.BROWSER_IGNORE_ACCENTS_IN_SEARCH, false));\n...\nif (mTruncateCheckBox.isChecked() != prefs.getBoolean(...)) editor.putBoolean(...)\n```\nSo single prefs, shared. So sharing is upstream behavior, not a bug.\n\nHmm, but the hint says \"each mode's display settings are now read from one shared place\" — that's likely describing the *columns* being read per mode from a shared object, i.e., the `BrowserColumns` class. The injected bug could be that both modes share the same column configuration object, meaning changes in one mode affect the other. But we tested and they didn't... unless the *reading* is shared and the *writing* isn't: e.g., the browser for Notes reads the cards column configuration from the shared place. But we saw Notes columns = notes defaults, distinct.\n\nHmm, unless the shared place is the *sort column index* and *current mode*. We tested sort separately.\n\nWait wait wait. Let me re-read: \"Card browser cards/notes toggle: each mode's display settings are now read from one shared place.\" Maybe the bug is: when the toggle is switched, the display settings do NOT update to the new mode's settings because they're read from one shared cached place (e.g., the browser doesn't reload columns when mode changes). But we saw columns update immediately after Save. Hmm, but what if it requires *reopening* the browser? We saw it update immediately (Cards→Notes at 11:26 showed notes columns right after Save). Fine.\n\nCould the bug be that the **toolbar name** \"cards shown\"/\"notes shown\" doesn't update? It did.\n\nI'm stuck on this hint. Let me examine other hints.\n\nDeck list arrow: \"each arrow's direction is now generated from the deck's stored collapsed flag\". Maybe the *icon direction* is right, but the **accessibility description** is wrong? We saw desc \"Expand\" for collapsed (right arrow) and \"Collapse\" for expanded (down arrow) — consistent. Hmm.\n\nCould the bug be that pressing the arrow *also* selects/opens the deck? It didn't.\n\nWhat about the arrow appearing for decks with no children? French has no arrow ✓.\n\nMaybe the bug is only with **filtered decks** or decks with special names? Hmm.\n\nMaybe the arrow direction is wrong for the **first render after app start** because the flag is read incorrectly at startup but corrected after a tap? We restarted (HOME + open_app) and arrows were correct. Hmm, that wasn't a cold restart though.\n\nLet me force-stop the app? We don't have adb. Could use Settings > apps > force stop via UI? That's heavy but possible. But HOME+open_app doesn't kill. Actually, swiping the app from recents kills it. Use APP_SWITCH then swipe up. Let's consider later.\n\nAdd note sorting: \"decks in the picker are now sorted by their full nested name.\" Maybe the injected bug: sorting is applied to the *flattened* list but the tree rendering still uses the original order? We saw sorted. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the bug appears in the **\"Filter decks\"** search results within the picker: when filtering, results might be sorted wrongly. Let's test: open Add note deck picker, tap Filter decks, type \"s\" — see matches sorted. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the \"deck chooser\" refers to the **deck spinner in the note editor when editing an existing note**? Same picker.\n\nLet me try to find bugs elsewhere in these areas with fresh eyes, especially things that would be easy to spot:\n\nDeck list: Are counts right? French 4, Spanish 4. Spanish parent includes Sub/Aaa/Deep (0). If a parent deck's count should include children, Spanish shows 4 = its own. Good. But wait: when Spanish is collapsed, shows 4. Sub/Aaa hidden. Fine.\n\nDeck list long-press: rename deck, delete deck, export. Bugs could lurk. But likely not.\n\nBrowser: \"Cards\"/\"Notes\" toggle aside, maybe the **\"Filter marked\"/\"Filter suspended\"** results are wrong. Let's test them quickly: tap Filter marked → browser should show 0 cards (or empty). Then Filter suspended similarly. These use search queries on the deck.\n\nAlso \"Preview\" with a selected card.\n\nAlso \"Select all\" and then editing multiple.\n\nAlso \"Find and replace\" - potentially destructive; allows regex replace across notes. Could test with a harmless no-match.\n\nAlso \"Create filtered deck\".\n\nLet's test Filter marked now (Cards mode, French). Cancel popup first."}
