{"type": "thinking", "text": "Filter \"spanish\" shows only \"Spanish\", no children. If the filter matched full names, Spanish::Aaa etc. would show (their full names contain \"spanish\"). But the UI might hide children when the parent matches? Or filter matches leaf only. In AnkiDroid, the deck filter (\"Filter decks\") searches the full name I believe. Hmm, this could be a bug, but it's the *filter*, not sorting.\n\nWait, let me think about what AnkiDroid's deck picker filter does: In the deck picker, the search looks at deck names; it expands matching decks and shows matching subdecks? I'm not sure. If the parent matches \"spanish\", showing only the parent (with its children hidden due to collapse?) is plausible: the filter shows \"Spanish\" and its expander, and you can expand to see children. Indeed there's a Collapse expander on Spanish. So children hidden because collapsed. If I expand, they may appear. Not a bug.\n\nOK. I'm spending a lot on this. Let me close the filter and picker.\n\nMaybe the injected bugs are actually hard to find but there. Let me re-examine the exact wording again:\n\n\"Changed in this build\n- Add note deck chooser: decks in the picker are now sorted by their full nested name.\n- Deck list expand/collapse arrows: each arrow's direction is now generated from the deck's stored collapsed flag.\n- Card browser cards/notes toggle: each mode's display settings are now read from one shared place.\"\n\nThese descriptions sound like *legit changes*. In these QA tasks, the repo has injected bugs, and the \"changed\" list describes the areas/code touched, which contain the bugs. The descriptions are probably paraphrases of the change (maybe the correct code). The bug is a subtle deviation.\n\nFor the add note deck chooser sort: Maybe the bug is that decks are sorted by full nested name but the sort omits the **current deck**'s siblings? Hmm. Or maybe sorting is correct in the *picker*, but the **Add note screen's initial deck selection** uses the first deck in the sorted list instead of the default/last deck! Wait — early on, the Add note screen initially opened with deck \"Spanish::Sub\" after I created Sub. But before creating sub, what was it? Let me recall: We first tapped Add from the deck list — hmm, that was after creating Sub. The first Add note we opened (at 11:24) showed deck Spanish::Sub, which was the last created deck. Standard AnkiDroid behavior: when creating a deck, it becomes the current deck; the Add screen defaults to current deck. That's fine.\n\nBut maybe the bug: the Add note deck chooser picks the *alphabetically first* deck when the current deck is not in the picker? Hmm.\n\nWait, here's a thought: The deck picker in the *note editor* when opened should scroll to / highlight the currently selected deck. With sorted list, maybe it highlights the wrong deck due to sorting (using index from unsorted list). We could test: current deck French; open picker; is French highlighted? In the screenshots, the picker showed rows with uniform background, no highlight visible. Hmm, maybe no highlight at all is normal.\n\nLet me test selecting a deck from a *collapsed parent*: e.g., open picker in editor, select Spanish (parent) — deck changes to Spanish. Save note? Maybe. Not bug.\n\nLet me shift: perhaps the bugs are around **data consistency** across screens. E.g., after adding the note, the deck list count French showed 4 ✓, browser All decks 8 ✓. After editing front, browser updated ✓.\n\nWhat about the **stats screen**? Not in scope.\n\nLet me test **note deletion** (via browser multi-select) since editing includes delete? Not explicitly, but \"adding and editing notes\" - deletion maybe not.\n\nMaybe the bug in editing: When you change the note's deck in the editor and save, does the browser/deck counts update? Let's test: edit testfront2, change deck to Spanish, save, verify browser shows it under Spanish and deck counts (French 3, Spanish 5), then move back to French. This tests the deck chooser selection in the editor (part of add/edit) and state consistency. If the deck chooser bug (sorting) exists, maybe selection works wrong (e.g., selecting a deck in sorted picker selects the wrong one due to index mismatch!). That's a classic bug: picker displays sorted list but returns the item at the pre-sort index → selecting \"Spanish\" actually sets \"French\" or \"Sub\". We haven't tested *selection* after sorting! We selected French earlier from the picker and the editor showed French — that worked. But maybe with nested decks, selecting a subdeck returns the wrong one? Let's test: In the editor picker, expand Spanish and select \"Aaa\" or \"Sub\"; check the editor shows the right deck. Earlier when I selected French it showed French. But maybe selecting Spanish::Aaa returns Spanish::Sub (sorted order vs original). Let's test this! Also selecting \"Spanish\" and \"All decks\" etc.\n\nLet me test: In the editor (currently browser), tap Add [2] (French default). Open deck picker, collapse/expand Spanish, select \"Aaa\", and check the editor's Deck label. If wrong → bug.\n\nWait, the picker from editor doesn't show \"All decks\" (only browser picker does). Fine.\n\nCurrently in deck picker filter. Cancel [42] to return to browser picker? Actually filter mode is within the browser deck picker. Press Cancel to close picker. Then tap Add.\n\nLet me do this test."}
