{"type": "thinking", "text": "Selecting Aaa correctly set Spanish::Aaa. So no index mismatch.\n\nHmm. Let me test selecting \"Sub\" too? Likely fine.\n\nLet me exit this Add screen (back, maybe no changes). Then think.\n\nMaybe I should inspect the browser's \"Filter by flag\" and \"Filter suspended\", \"Preview\", \"Select all\" quickly for obvious failures. Also the *deck list* long-press menu. And the *add note* \"Type\" spinner (only Basic). Hmm.\n\nActually, wait. Let me revisit the possibility that the bugs are in *state persistence* across app restart, particularly the cards/notes mode and deck collapsed flags. We only backgrounded the app once, which may not restart the activity's process. If the bug is that the collapsed flag is stored only in memory (e.g., in a static variable) and the arrow is generated from it, a cold restart would reset all decks to expanded and arrows wrong. The hint \"stored collapsed flag\" suggests DB storage. Let me force-stop the app via recents swipe, then relaunch. That's a real test.\n\nHow to force-stop: press APP_SWITCH, then swipe the app card up. Then open_app. Let's try.\n\nBut before that, finish the Add editor: back out."}
