{"type": "thinking", "text": "\"Undo Select Deck\" persists even after leaving and returning to browser. In AnkiDroid, the undo menu shows the last undoable collection operation. \"Select Deck\" is presumably an operation from the config/deck selection? Hmm, in Anki's backend, changing the current deck is stored in the config table (not undoable?). Actually \"Select Deck\" is a valid undoable op in AnkiDroid when you change the *deck of a note*? Hmm, but we haven't changed a note's deck. Wait, in AnkiDroid, there's an operation `SelectDeck`? I recall AnkiDroid had an undoable operation for changing the deck of a note via the editor? Hmm.\n\nHold on: When I earlier switched the *browser deck filter* from French to All decks, the menu then showed \"Undo Select Deck\". Did the browser perform a collection operation? In the new AnkiDroid browser, changing the selected deck filter may call `set_current_deck` on the collection, which is an undoable operation in Anki 2.1.50+? Possibly! In Anki, changing the current deck is saved in config and might be undoable. Hmm, maybe. Actually in Anki Desktop, changing the deck selection in the browser adds an undo entry \"Select Deck\"? I don't think so... In AnkiDroid, there is indeed an undo item \"Select Deck\" that appears when the current deck changes (because AnkiDroid's undo framework pushes it). I've seen users complain about \"Undo Select Deck\". Not a bug per se.\n\nTapping it might revert the current deck to the previous one, which could change the browser filter. Let's not.\n\nLet me think about the injected bugs differently: maybe I should compare against the *expected* behavior described in the hints, and the bug might be in the **reverse** direction:\n\n1. \"Add note deck chooser: decks in the picker are now sorted by their full nested name.\" Maybe the injected bug: the picker sorts by **name length** or by **deck ID**, but our observations were alphabetical. Could our decks coincidentally be in ID order? IDs: French created first, Spanish second, then Sub (id3), Aaa (id4), Deep (id5). Sorted order observed: French, Spanish, Aaa, Sub — that's alphabetical, not ID (which would be Sub then Aaa). Within Spanish, ID order = Sub, Aaa; observed Aaa, Sub. So sorting is definitely alphabetical, not ID.\n\nMaybe sorted by full nested name *including* \"::\" gives \"Spanish::Aaa\" < \"Spanish::Sub\" ✓. Case okay.\n\n2. \"Deck list arrows...\" observed correct.\n\n3. \"Cards/notes toggle...\" observed columns/sort separate, truncate shared.\n\nHmm, all three seem to work as described! Is it possible this build has bugs elsewhere and these are fine? The task says \"sweep these areas\" and there are likely injected bugs. But maybe the bugs are subtle in ways I haven't exercised:\n- Add note deck chooser: sorting with decks that have *different depths* or a **filter** (we saw filter results maybe wrong).\n- Deck arrows: maybe after *renaming*.\n- Cards/notes: maybe when using the *search saved* or *filter*.\n\nWait, maybe the deck arrow bug: the arrow direction is generated from the stored collapsed flag, BUT the *expand/collapse tap on the arrow uses a different flag*, so after app restart they desync. We tested navigate-away. Let me test a cold restart via Settings > Force stop, since recents swipe failed. Actually, another way to force stop: long-press app icon on launcher → App info → Force stop. That's doable:\n- HOME\n- long-press AnkiDroid icon? The launcher has no AnkiDroid icon visible on this home screen (only Gallery, Contacts, WebView Browser Tester, Camera, plus search widget). Hmm, AnkiDroid was opened via open_app tool directly. There may be an app drawer. We could use Settings app: swipe up to app drawer? Or Settings via quick settings? The device likely has Settings app accessible. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, `open_app` may relaunch/recreate the activity without killing the process. Not a true cold start.\n\nMaybe test rotation persistence of arrows: rotating might recreate the activity and reload flags. Let's test: currently Spanish expanded, Aaa collapsed. Rotate to landscape and check arrow states. We already rotated earlier with expanded Spanish and it stayed. But that was before the 3-level setup. Let's rotate now? We're in browser; go to deck list first. Eh.\n\nI think I need to find a clearer bug. Let me examine other UI elements for anomalies.\n\nOne thing I noticed: In the deck list, after creating \"Spanish::Aaa\", the Spanish deck remained at 4 cards. But also, the *Add note* screen defaulted to \"Spanish::Aaa\" — the newly created deck became current. Standard.\n\nAnother observation: In the *browser* deck picker, the \"All decks\" option appears at top, then French, Spanish. In the *Add note* picker, there's NO \"All decks\" option. That's expected (can't add to all decks).\n\nAnother: The *Add note* picker shows \"Default\" deck? Not shown. Hmm, wait: the precondition says decks Spanish/French; there's no Default shown anywhere. But the browser initially showed \"Default | 0 cards shown\". That suggests a \"Default\" deck exists (id 1) with 0 cards but is **not displayed** in the deck list or pickers. In Anki, the Default deck usually always exists. AnkiDroid hides empty \"Default\" deck? I recall AnkiDroid shows Default only if it has cards. So fine.\n\nHmm, what about the deck list \"Check\" menu item — not.\n\nMaybe the injected bug for the deck list is about the arrow *ordering/hierarchy* when a deck name contains \"::\" but the parent deck doesn't exist? Not relevant.\n\nLet me look at the \"Add note\" and \"Edit note\" screens more: The note editor has a \"Deck:\" row. Is there a \"sort by full nested name\" bug in the **note editor's deck picker when opened from the browser selected deck filter**? Already similar.\n\nWhat about the **\"Add\" button in the card browser** vs the **FAB Add** producing different default decks? Could be a bug: from browser with Spanish filter, Add might default to the *last used deck* rather than the current filter deck. We saw from browser (French filter) Add opened with French. Then later Add from browser (All decks) opened with Spanish::Aaa::Deep (last created deck/current deck), not \"All decks\" (can't add to All). Hmm! Wait, that's interesting: The browser filter was \"All decks\" but the Add screen defaulted to \"Spanish::Aaa::Deep\" — the current deck in the collection, not the browser filter. Hmm, what should it be? In AnkiDroid, the \"Add\" from browser uses the currently selected deck in the browser? I believe it uses the deck of the currently selected card or the current deck. Not sure.\n\nLet's test a clearer scenario: Browser filter = French, Add note → deck French (we saw this at 11:28). Browser filter = All decks, Add → current deck (Spanish::Aaa::Deep). Ambiguous.\n\nLet's try browser filter = Spanish, Add → Spanish? Probably.\n\nAnother possible bug: The Add note screen's deck chooser in *edit* mode vs *add* mode. In edit mode, changing the deck and saving moves the note. Let's test that to check consistency. I'll use testfront2 → move to Sub → verify counts/browser → move back to French. This touches \"editing notes\" and \"deck list\" consistency. Let's do it.\n\nCurrently browser Notes mode All decks. Tap testfront2 [10]."}
