{"type": "thinking", "text": "Order: apple, French, Spanish, Aaa, Sub. Case-insensitive ✓ (apple first). Sorting correct.\n\nHmm, but wait: Sub is shown under Spanish (Spanish expanded, Aaa collapsed). Fine.\n\nSo the deck picker sort works.\n\nNow I've added \"apple\" deck; need to delete it eventually. Also need to delete Sub, Aaa/Deep, note testfront2, restore note sort and mode.\n\nBefore cleanup, let me consider the cards/notes toggle bug one final time. Maybe test the \"Ignore accents\" toggle: set it in Cards mode, check it persists and whether it also appears checked in Notes mode (shared). If AnkiDroid is supposed to have a single global \"ignore accents\", then fine. Hmm.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the phrasing: \"each mode's display settings are now read from one shared place.\" Perhaps in the *browser*, the \"Cards\" and \"Notes\" mode have separate display settings **for columns**, and the change centralized the *default column list* into one place. The injected bug might be that the **default columns for Notes mode are the Cards columns** (or vice versa) when no custom columns saved. But we saw default notes columns: Sort Field, Note Type, Cards, Tags — that's correct for notes. Cards default: Sort Field, Card Type, Due, Deck — correct.\n\nHmm, hold on. Are those the *default* AnkiDroid columns? Let me recall AnkiDroid's default cards columns: \"Sort Field\", \"Card Type\", \"Due\", \"Deck\"? In new AnkiDroid 2.16, default columns for cards mode: \"Sort Field\", \"Card Type\", \"Due\", \"Deck\". For notes mode: \"Sort Field\", \"Note Type\", \"Cards\", \"Tags\". Yes, I believe so.\n\nOK.\n\nMaybe the bug is in the **toolbar deck filter dropdown** after toggling notes/cards: e.g., notes mode should show note counts in the deck picker? No.\n\nLet me try another angle: maybe the injected bug in the cards/notes toggle is that the **\"Cards\"/\"Notes\" radio in the options dialog is disabled or doesn't reflect saved state after a reload** — we tested it reflects. \n\nCould the bug be about **search query** when switching modes: e.g., a search query containing a card-only field fails in notes mode? Eh.\n\nGiven the hints, maybe this build's three changes are actually all fine and the bugs are in *other* aspects of the same areas. Let me hunt in the browser: \"Create filtered deck\", \"Find and replace\", \"Select all\", \"Preview\", \"Save search\". Let me test \"Select all\" and a bulk action (e.g., \"Change deck\" / \"Delete notes\"?) — could reveal bugs in multi-select UI. But these are outside the changed hints.\n\nActually, wait. Maybe I should reconsider the *truncate content* sharing as a genuine bug. Let me check AnkiDroid's actual current behavior by using the app's Settings? Not available.\n\nHmm, let me look at the **\"Browsing\"** section: \"Ignore accents in search (slower)\" — this is a search prefs, global, fine.\n\nWhat about the checkbox states when toggling mode *before* saving: we saw truncate remains checked/unchecked across radio toggles. If the app intended per-mode, the checkbox should change when you switch. But since the *saved* state is shared, it doesn't. Hmm.\n\nI recall now! In AnkiDroid, the BrowserOptions has a **per-mode \"cards/notes\" preference** but the *truncate* setting is indeed global. Let me search my memory of `Prefs.java`: `BROWSER_TRUNCATE_CONTENT = \"browserTruncateContent\"`, `BROWSER_IGNORE_ACCENTS_IN_SEARCH`, `BROWSER_CARDS_MODE`. Yes only one truncate. So shared is correct.\n\nOK, then maybe the third hint's bug is: \"each mode's display settings are now read from one shared place\" → the **columns are read from one shared place**, i.e., the Manage columns screen shows the wrong mode's columns in a specific flow (the unsaved radio state). Hmm.\n\nActually, let me look at the AnkiDroid browser options implementation: When you toggle the radio group, the dialog likely calls `updateRadioButtons()` or `onCheckedChanged` which updates the columns button? There's a known behavior: Changing mode in browser options **immediately** updates the browser (the dialog might not have Save/Cancel in older versions, but here it does). Hmm, here there are Save/Cancel buttons, unusual for AnkiDroid BrowserOptions (older versions had a \"OK/Cancel\"). In AnkiDroid 2.17, BrowserOptions has a toolbar \"Save\" and discards on back? Hmm.\n\nLet me test the *Cancel* path of browser options: change mode to Notes but press Cancel; verify the browser stays Cards. That's a reversal test. If Cancel doesn't revert (because the radio change applied settings immediately from the shared place), that's a bug! We haven't tested Cancel after changing the radio. Let's test: currently we're in Add note screen; back out. Then in browser (Notes mode currently? Let's see: the browser was Notes mode with filter Aaa. Wait, after cleanup steps, browser mode is still Notes (we never switched back). Actually we're in Add note editor now from deck list. Back twice to deck list. Then browser: currently Notes, deck Aaa.\n\nTest: Options > switch Cards > Cancel > check mode remains Notes. If it becomes Cards, that's a bug (Cancel not reverting). Similarly Save persists. Also test truncate toggling + Cancel.\n\nLet's do it."}
